hsw's own timing, measured (docs/wasm-hcaptcha-measurement.md, "Timing"):

  clock-probe.js   every performance.now() / Date.now() value read in
                   hCaptcha's frames, logged as "TMREC <frame> p<v> d<v> ..."
                   (batches of 120: the engine keeps console lines < 2 KB).
                   Chromium: chrome-demo.py --init clock-probe.js > out.txt;
                   simulator: VITA_SIM_INJECT=clock-probe.js sim-demo.sh DIR,
                   then grep TMREC from DIR's netsurf.log.
  clocks.py        counts, exact-tenth share and deltas: clocks.py out.txt ...
  event-loop.html  rAF interval, setTimeout(0) x10 (the nesting clamp),
                   setTimeout(50), microtask and MessageChannel latency --
                   open it in each engine; the title holds the result.
  clean-tenths.js  --init: Chromium's performance.now() in exact tenths, as
                   this engine's (patch 270): Chromium still passes.
  late-timers.js   --init: Chromium's timers a frame late, as this engine's
                   were before patch 281: Chromium still passes.
